   "span": "full",
   "emphasis": "panel",
   "perspectives": [],
   "detail_spec": null,
   "content": "**2. Are the DATA domain's own metrics moving?**  The data governance program defines six metrics.  Three have a live measure below: *Percentage of Data Assets with Designated Owner* (Data Asset Ownership, a direct measure), *Catalog Registration Coverage* (Governance Classification Coverage and Catalog Freshness, a partial measure until discovery scanning runs) and *Lineage Coverage for Critical Data Elements* (Solution Design Context, a proxy: the first hop from an asset to the design it implements, not an end-to-end lineage path).",
