  {
   "position": 11,
   "ref": "Data Quality Not Yet Measured",
   "kind": "text",
   "title": "Data Quality Not Yet Measured",
   "span": "full",
   "emphasis": "panel",
   "perspectives": [
    "governance",
    "steward"
   ],
   "detail_spec": null,
   "content": "**Not yet measured: data quality.**  Three of the DATA domain's metrics — *Critical Data Element Quality Expectation Coverage*, *Data Quality Rule Pass Rate* (target 98% or above) and *Open Data Quality Issues by Age* (target: nothing older than seven days on critical data) — need automated quality rule results and a record of the issues they raise.  The clinical trials pipeline in `2. clinical-trials` runs quality checks, but their results are not yet recorded in the catalog in a form these tiles can count.  Until they are, the honest answer to *how good is our data?* is *we cannot yet say*, and closing this gap is the next priority for Erin Overview and Peter Profile.",
   "note": null,
   "restricted": false,
   "restricted_element": null,
   "reason": null,
   "report_guid": null,
   "report": null,
   "spec": null,
   "spec_source": null,
   "runnable": null,
   "refusal": null,
   "result": null,
   "error": null
  },
